# Copy to `.env` and fill in. The playground reads this on startup.
# ── LLM vendor ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Pick ONE of the two blocks below.

# A) OpenAI-compatible endpoint — any vendor speaking the OpenAI Chat Completions
#    protocol (DeepSeek / Qwen / Moonshot / Zhipu / ...).
LLM_BASE_URL=https://open.bigmodel.cn/api/paas/v4
LLM_API_KEY=
LLM_MODEL=

# B) Fully offline fake LLM — zero key, zero network.
# USE_FAKE_LLM=1

# ── Optional: production backends ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# `make playground-prod` sets these itself and also spins up the containers —
# you only need them here if you run outside the Makefile.
# PRODAGENT_BACKEND=prod
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://postgres:prodagent@localhost:5433/prodagent
# REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6390/0
# NEO4J_URI=bolt://localhost:7687
# NEO4J_USER=neo4j
# NEO4J_PASSWORD=password
# QDRANT_URL=http://localhost:6333
# QDRANT_COLLECTION=prodagent
